verdicts.revised_change:
List description: 'A unit-wide gauge that shapes how the unit plays. A card has at most one.' -> 'A gauge or a purse that limits how the unit acts: a gauge on the unit, or currency spent each time it acts. A card has at most one.'
New term: {"id": "pay-per-use", "label": "Pay per use", "description": "Its abilities or special shots cost currency each time they are used, paid from the player's or the team's purse rather than a gauge on the unit, so using them competes with buying units and upgrades. The unit's price and gear bought once per life do not count. Abilities still record their cooldown band as usual."}
Run npm run docs and vocab-diff.

New term: {"id": "thermal", "label": "Thermal sight", "description": "Within its sight it sees enemies through smoke, foliage and darkness, though not through walls. It does not reveal cloaked, stealthy or burrowed enemies; that is the detector.", "classes": ["infantry", "vehicle", "walker", "hover", "aircraft", "drone"]}
List description, append: 'A view the player can switch to at any time, with no cooldown or cost, counts as always-on.'
The sensors group decides together with its loadout rule. Under decision 1A what it sees the whole team sees, so it counters lay-smoke, not cloak. Run npm run docs.
